{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493396-opinion-question-lich-legacy","id":1493396,"title":"Opinion Question - Lich Legacy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-20T03:33:22-07:00","id":1493396,"title":"Opinion Question - Lich Legacy","content":"I'm writing up a Lich Legacy, the capstone of which allows you to cheat death by turning into a Goetia-Ghost abomination upon physical demise and claim a new body.<br /> <br /> Now, I have two visions of how this could go. I'd appreciate any opinions on which would work best, both in terms of being in line with the setting and with the crunch of making a Legacy.<br /> <br /> 1. The disembodied Lich just outright hunts down and claims the new body ala 1e's Steal Body. Boring, but mechanically simple beyond maybe having to work out an XP refund for lost Physical Attributes. <br /> <br /> 2. This... fragment isn't truely a Mage anymore, but whomever it &quot;claims&quot; will immediately Awaken to the Lich's Path, and they'll be locked into the Legacy. The Lich has to enter the victim's Oneiros and subsume the victim's Daimon, giving the new Mage hazy but usable memories and knowledge to work off of. It's the more complicated option to work out mechanically, especially in regards to Gnosis and Arcana for the new Mage. The closest examples I can think of in media are Rand and Mat in The Wheel of Time, or Oscar/Ozpin in RWBY.<br /> <br /> The lesser choice for either is to just find a Life Master to create a body for you, but then you're physical form is dispellable, and your probably Soulless in option 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T04:45:11-07:00","id":1493399,"title":"","content":"If this is a Legacy, as opposed to a \u2018Night Horror\u2019 (ie. an antagonist largely intended to be Storyteller-controlled), you\u2019d want some player-facing Attainments in the lower ranks too. Any ideas?<br /> <br /> The second idea looks a lot like a Morphean from 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T05:00:07-07:00","id":1493400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493396-opinion-question-lich-legacy?p=1493399#post1493399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this is a Legacy, as opposed to a \u2018Night Horror\u2019 (ie. an antagonist largely intended to be Storyteller-controlled), you\u2019d want some player-facing Attainments in the lower ranks too. Any ideas?<br /> <br /> The second idea looks a lot like a Morphean from 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind Legacy for Mysterium or Moros. All Attainments require both Mind and Death, and there's no Optional track.<br /> <br /> Initiate - no solid idea yet<br /> <br /> Apprentice - Combined Mental Shield and Soul Armour, Advanced Duration<br /> <br /> Disciple - an involved version of Astral Grimoire that creates ephemeral Grimoires and Libraries in Twilight. A Library can also be an Advanced Library if the Mage has a relevant Goetia in their Onieros. Lasting Duration Reach effect. They exist in a state halfway between Mind- and Death-attuned Twilight, constantly flickering between the two in erratic fractal shards. They can only be properly read using a Mind+Death Unveiling spell, and are otherwise rambling gibberish.<br /> <br /> Adept - variation of Transubstantiation that temporarily transforms Ghosts and Death-Twilight Phenomenon into Goetia and Mind-Twilight Phenomenon. Willing sentient subjects are treated as having (Withstand-2). Expounding off of Goetic Evocation, this means you could thus intergrate a former ghost into your Onieros, at least temporarily.<br /> <br /> Master - the &quot;Cheat Death&quot; ability that I 'd like an opinion on. I'm basing a lot of it on the Reach effect of Goetic Evocation; &quot;the Goetia integrates itself with the caster\u2019s psyche and becomes a true part of him for the Duration of the spell, influencing his attitudes, behaviors, and even mannerisms&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 09-20-2022, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T05:25:48-07:00","id":1493401,"title":"","content":"A Moros Lich with Mind. Sounds like an aggresively applied Ship of Theseus; you slowly and surgically replace a victim\u2019s psyche until they might as well be your mental clone, then you smoothly take over the \u2018sleeve\u2019. <br /> <br /> (In hindsight, that reads a lot like a Ventrue. Or one of the Unchained.)<br /> <br /> Maybe the Attainments summon Goetia out of someone\u2019s Oneiros to consume them, then place bits of your own to replace the gap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T05:47:54-07:00","id":1493403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493396-opinion-question-lich-legacy?p=1493401#post1493401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Moros Lich with Mind. Sounds like an aggresively applied Ship of Theseus; you slowly and surgically replace a victim\u2019s psyche until they might as well be your mental clone, then you smoothly take over the \u2018sleeve\u2019. <br /> <br /> (In hindsight, that reads a lot like a Ventrue. Or one of the Unchained.)<br /> <br /> Maybe the Attainments summon Goetia out of someone\u2019s Oneiros to consume them, then place bits of your own to replace the gap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, I was leaning more toward less... proactive Lichdom. Reincarnation rather than becoming a faceless legion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T12:27:23-07:00","id":1493418,"title":"","content":"2. Is more interesting in some ways, but also isn't lichdom, right? Of you lose your soul and become a fragment of what you once were... It seems more like a messed up way to grow replacement parts for your legacy.<br /> <br /> But since newly awakened mages begin with Gnosis 1, it is a bit of a ghostly master and (not even initiated) legacy member... <br /> <br /> This is more interesting because what happens when the fragment is exorcised, but the awakened mage is still a member of the legacy... Or they die and now you may need to find two bodies for both the original fragment and the new one. <br /> <br /> How much independence does the host mage have? Can they fight to remove their 'mentor', can the mentor lie quietly in the Temenos or some sleeper Oneirous until they find the right partner (making it more like Geist:the Sin-Eater's titular character).<br /> <br /> Being an actual awakened ghost entity with the ability to claim a sleeper body would be tough enough to pull off, but then you have to find a way to protect yourself, grow a legacy? <br /> <br /> Nowhere near as interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 09-20-2022, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T12:38:15-07:00","id":1493421,"title":"","content":"What does it mean for a character to become both a ghost and a goetia?<br /> <br /> For that matter, if it's about lichs, why is the more elaborate option one that doesn't really allow the mage to preserve very much of themselves?<br /> <br /> If they're becoming an ephemeral being, a spell wouldn't have to be necessary to possess somebody, Manifestations can do that. Possession doesn't let one retain powers, but Claim does, although given how that turns the subject into a monster with Dread Powers rather than quite having the power the possess in their original form...well there are a few options there. One is to have the lich be somebody who inhabits mortal bodies in order to experience human sensation, but does a creepy folkloric thing of projecting their spiritual side out in order to wield power. Another is to come up with a custom Manifestation that basically amounts to &quot;all magic (and other powers if they apply) still accessible when body is acquired. The last is to say that they do indeed trade in the full flexibility of Arcana for a set of Dread Powers in exchange for physicality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T14:34:33-07:00","id":1493432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493396-opinion-question-lich-legacy?p=1493418#post1493418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Is more interesting in some ways, but also isn't lichdom, right? Of you lose your soul and become a fragment of what you once were... It seems more like a messed up way to grow replacement parts for your legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493396-opinion-question-lich-legacy?p=1493421#post1493421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For that matter, if it's about lichs, why is the more elaborate option one that doesn't really allow the mage to preserve very much of themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div> For the internal logic? &quot;We aren't <i>really</i> Liches, we just ensure that we have a successor for our work!&quot;<br /> <br /> Meta reason? I thought a reincarnation take on Lichdom might be interesting to try and hammer out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493396-opinion-question-lich-legacy?p=1493421#post1493421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does it mean for a character to become both a ghost and a goetia?</div> </div> </div> </div>Being a Morphean that can enter and exit the Astral, was my main intent. Also existing in both Death and Mind Twilight, which is probably more of a vulnerability than an asset.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493396-opinion-question-lich-legacy?p=1493421#post1493421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they're becoming an ephemeral being, a spell wouldn't have to be necessary to possess somebody, Manifestations can do that. Possession doesn't let one retain powers, but Claim does, although given how that turns the subject into a monster with Dread Powers rather than quite having the power the possess in their original form...well there are a few options there. One is to have the lich be somebody who inhabits mortal bodies in order to experience human sensation, but does a creepy folkloric thing of projecting their spiritual side out in order to wield power. Another is to come up with a custom Manifestation that basically amounts to &quot;all magic (and other powers if they apply) still accessible when body is acquired. The last is to say that they do indeed trade in the full flexibility of Arcana for a set of Dread Powers in exchange for physicality.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ephemeral state was meant to be less like becoming a Morphean and more like becoming an Unwoven Coadjutor and Past Life from Exalted. The newly Awakened Mage becomes your new character, and your old one becomes a voice in your head that slowly infests your other Goetia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493396-opinion-question-lich-legacy?p=1493418#post1493418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But since newly awakened mages begin with Gnosis 1, it is a bit of a ghostly master and (not even initiated) legacy member...</div> </div> </div> </div>They're already Initiated, but don't get any of the benefits until they reach the appropriate Gnosis and Arcana levels. Which would be a reason for their existence to disgust other Mages just as much as the obvious lichdom. You've not only co-opted someone else to survive (after a fashion), but you've denied them the personal growth that comes with shaping their soul under their own agency.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493396-opinion-question-lich-legacy?p=1493418#post1493418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is more interesting because what happens when the fragment is exorcised, but the awakened mage is still a member of the legacy... Or they die and now you may need to find two bodies for both the original fragment and the new one.</div> </div> </div> </div> I lean towards the interpretation that the Daimon replacement is Lasting, so it can't be exorcised without inflicting Daimonlessness on the victim. Similarly, there's a period of vulnerability where the Lich can be killed normally, until they regain Gnosis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493396-opinion-question-lich-legacy?p=1493418#post1493418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much independence does the host mage have? Can they fight to remove their 'mentor',</div> </div> </div> </div> You can check out any time you like, but you can never leave. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493396-opinion-question-lich-legacy?p=1493418#post1493418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the mentor lie quietly in the Temenos or some sleeper Oneirous until they find the right partner (making it more like Geist:the Sin-Eater's titular character).</div> </div> </div> </div> Current draft has them able to sustain themselves for up to a year, although they can &quot;reset&quot; that Duration by taking over a Create Life host.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493396-opinion-question-lich-legacy?p=1493418#post1493418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being an actual awakened ghost entity with the ability to claim a sleeper body would be tough enough to pull off, but then you have to find a way to protect yourself, grow a legacy? <br /> <br /> Nowhere near as interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Bodysnatcher archetype is horrifying, but pretty bland.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 09-20-2022, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T19:08:57-07:00","id":1493612,"title":"","content":"That makes me wonder, how could one create a spell that replicates the regenerations The Doctor uses to reincarnate ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-25T05:34:33-07:00","id":1493665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493396-opinion-question-lich-legacy?p=1493612#post1493612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes me wonder, how could one create a spell that replicates the regenerations The Doctor uses to reincarnate ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Go the Exalted 3e Larceny route, and have them assume the life of a Masque upon being killed? Some combination of Mind, Fate, and/or Death most likely. Might be able to get some milage out of Create Life, but that's a stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-25T06:02:31-07:00","id":1493666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493396-opinion-question-lich-legacy?p=1493612#post1493612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes me wonder, how could one create a spell that replicates the regenerations The Doctor uses to reincarnate ?</div> </div> </div> </div>First, a (homebrew) Life spell that overhauls and reconfigurates a living creature\u2019s body. Life 5, though maybe an argument can be made for Life 4 with a stretch.<br /> <br /> Then \u2018hang\u2019 it with a casting of Hung Spell (Time 2) at an indefinite Duration. But set Hung Spell with a Conditional Duration of \u2018When I die.\u2019","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-25T14:41:08-07:00","id":1493678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493396-opinion-question-lich-legacy?p=1493666#post1493666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First, a (homebrew) Life spell that overhauls and reconfigurates a living creature\u2019s body. Life 5, though maybe an argument can be made for Life 4 with a stretch.<br /> <br /> Then \u2018hang\u2019 it with a casting of Hung Spell (Time 2) at an indefinite Duration. But set Hung Spell with a Conditional Duration of \u2018When I die.\u2019</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe a combination of Temporal Stutter in there too, to protect you from being re-gibbed by whatever killed you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-25T18:21:18-07:00","id":1493696,"title":"","content":"Probably throw some Death into the spell too, otherwise you will suffer soul loss after being revived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T02:15:54-07:00","id":1493707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493396-opinion-question-lich-legacy?p=1493666#post1493666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First, a (homebrew) Life spell that overhauls and reconfigurates a living creature\u2019s body. Life 5, though maybe an argument can be made for Life 4 with a stretch.<br /> <br /> Then \u2018hang\u2019 it with a casting of Hung Spell (Time 2) at an indefinite Duration. But set Hung Spell with a Conditional Duration of \u2018When I die.\u2019</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure life 4 is all you need, since you are not Making or Unmaking anything, can't use Life 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T03:00:42-07:00","id":1493709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493396-opinion-question-lich-legacy?p=1493707#post1493707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty sure life 4 is all you need, since you are not Making or Unmaking anything, can't use Life 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assigned Life 5 (Making) after noticing a tendency for assigning \u2018generating sufficiently advanced and complex Patterns out of existant simpler Patterns\u2019 as Making, even though \u2018Pattern A to/from Pattern B\u2019 is usually Patterning.<br /> <br /> (Spirit 5 Birth Spirit says it coaxes dormant Essence into a newborn spirit, while Matter 5 Self-Repairing Machine imbues an existant object with self-healing.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}